@startuml
' Figure 20-4: one rewrite firing as a metered COMM cascade on the host reducer. Generic
' over the rule families: the VISIBLE fire is ONE COMM; the congruence cascade (only when
' the RHS needs substitution congruence) is a run of internal tau COMMs; every COMM is
' metered by the interpreter's own cost accounting. The beta-substitution depth is in doc 19.
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5568
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A7A7A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F4F4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A7A7A
  ParticipantFontColor #202020
}

title Figure 20-4 — One rewrite fires as a metered COMM cascade\nvisible fire = ONE COMM; congruence cascade = <latex>\tau</latex>; every COMM charges phlogiston

participant "set automaton\n(match, in Rho)" as SA #C6E0F5
participant "<latex>\sigma</latex>-receiver\n(firing)" as SIG #FDE8D5
participant "congruence receiver(s)\ne-graph closed at compile;\nsubst TRS at runtime" as CON #E6DBF2
participant "RSpace + cost meter\n(f1r3node)" as RS #A7D8B6
participant "@OUT\n(observed reduct)" as OUT #FEF7E0

group <latex>\tau^{*}</latex> prefix — reflect + spread + locate (internal)
  SA -> RS : produce loc:/cap: head tags (spread <latex>[\![t]\!]</latex>)
  RS --> SA : consume, capture <latex>\sigma</latex>  (sa: <latex>\tau</latex> COMMs)
end

SA -[#C05621]-> SIG : <b>accept COMM — the ONE visible fire</b>
RS -[#2F855A]-> RS : charge send/receive/match cost (phlo)

group <latex>\tau</latex> cascade — congruence (only if the RHS needs substitution)
  SIG -> CON : <latex>[\![R]\!]\sigma</latex> requires substitution congruence
  CON -> RS : reserved-channel COMMs (subst TRS)
  RS --> CON : each COMM charges phlo
  CON --> SIG : normal-form subterms rejoin (atomic join)
end

SIG -[#2F855A]-> OUT : <latex>\mathtt{out}\,!\,([\![R]\!]\sigma)</latex> — the reduct
note over RS, OUT #E6F4EA
  Metered by construction: every COMM passes through the interpreter's
  cost accounting — no manual hook, no unmetered host pre-computation.
  Tests set Cost::unsafe_max (run.rs:458), so metering is OFF while they
  assert functional results. <latex>\beta</latex>-substitution depth: doc 19.
end note
@enduml
